From: Gabriel Duarte Guerra <72227489+GabriWar@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: guard against NULL entries in ttm->pages during
 unpopulate

amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate() walks ttm->pages[] and writes pages[i]->mapping
without checking for NULL. If a GPU command fails partway through, the buffer
object can be left partially populated and cleanup dereferences a NULL page:

  RIP: 0010:amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate+0x77/0xd0 [amdgpu]
  CR2: 0000000000000018
  RAX: 0000000000000000  RBX: ffff8c72d0b6e180  RCX: 0000000000000000
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception

CR2 = 0x18 is the offset of struct page::mapping, confirming pages[i] was NULL.

This matters on the BC-250 because GPU command failures on gfx1013 are routine
while the compute defect is unresolved, and every one of them risked taking the
whole blade down. With the guard the failing process dies but the machine
survives. It is containment, not a fix for the abort itself.

Hunk regenerated 2026-08-17 against linux-cachyos-bore-7.0.9 (7.0.9-1 tarball)
and byte-verified against the deployed build2 tree on blade 15 (a fleet blade,
snapshot snap-8fe794e8).

Signed-off-by: Gabriel Duarte Guerra <72227489+GabriWar@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ttm.c
@@ -1255,8 +1255,11 @@ static void amdgpu_ttm_tt_unpopulate(struct ttm_device *bdev,
 	if (ttm->page_flags & TTM_TT_FLAG_EXTERNAL)
 		return;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ttm->num_pages; ++i)
-		ttm->pages[i]->mapping = NULL;
+	for (i = 0; i < ttm->num_pages; ++i) {
+		struct page *p = ttm->pages[i];
+		if (p)
+			p->mapping = NULL;
+	}
 
 	adev = amdgpu_ttm_adev(bdev);
 
